xd on OS-9 -- what was changed=============================Nothing.  John Walker's XD revision 1, comp.sources.misc volume 37 issue56 (1991), compiled unchanged with `cc -qm' and runs as posted.  ORIG/holds the release; xd.c beside it is the same file.It is kept here so that the program has a source tree like itsneighbours, and so that anyone rebuilding it does not have to work outwhich of the files in ORIG/ is the one the recipe names.The author's own aim, from ORIG/README: "XD is written to be as portableas possible.  It does assume that file I/O is not subjected to end ofline translation" -- which is true here.